readme='''# Frozen RNAcentral v23 pointer publication review\n\nC2 completed normally; the staged master is81,054,784taskviews /82,141shards /37,333,973,228taskbytes. It adds54,732,469train-onlynative priors, preserving445,486oldRNApilot views once and5,828,304Rfam reuse views without duplication. Existing v22 remains the current pointer.\n\nThis package is NOT APPROVED and has executed no publisher. `execution-plan.json` binds every source/code/dependency/test input plus exact current intake JSONs and the complete oldv22handoff files. `frozen-small-inputs/` contains byte-exact snapshots. No giant index rerun was made: the reviewed C2 closing-hash path and normal receipt are retained, with exact current stat/no-journal checks. Source/task/sidecar hashes were already proven by C1/C2 and the C2 closure.\n\nThe proposed one-shot guard calls the EXISTING publisher only after a separate root approval with exact scope/plan/script hashes, unchanged input pins, absent old RNA owners, original clock,64GiB hardware floor plus1GiB write reserve, hostRAM/CPU/nice guards, fresh new output namespaces and exact binary backups of the only two mutable targets. See `future-exact-argv.json`; create its log exclusively. The whole process is bounded by120s internal /150s outer (+15s kill), CPU27/nice10,3GiB address space, noGPU/network. No actual job launch is present.\n\nMutable targets after future approval: `planning/data_intake_progress.json` and `configs/dataset_acquisition_queue.json` only. Exact prepublication bytes are independently snapshotted here and must also be copied to the planned NEW run/backups paths before the original publisher is called. Five handoff JSONs are new-only. All oldv22handoffs, stagedv23source/task/group files, indexes, logs, checkpoints, model files and weights remain immutable. Any failure retains new files/backups/failure evidence; no retry, cleanup or rollback is authorized. A crash between the two original pointer writes can leave a partial pointer update; backups and failure diagnostics make it reviewable and any repair requires a separate exact review.\n\nPostchecks enforce exact old+new counts, unchanged validation/test allocations, primary-family sum, preserved114inventory IDs/order and source evidence, declared nested mutation allowlists, no unrelated field edits, and false/null full-readiness, global-leakage-safe, model-use/training, mixture-weight and tokenizer/exposure claims. Native characters remain distinct from model tokens. ReferenceRNA gives no physical material/modified-chemistry/function/ADMET measurement or independent experiment. No final expanded-dataset readiness signature exists.\n\nThe live model owner may continue editing its own modules. AST inventory reads hash each file and record before/after stability; it never imports a model or establishes reader/neural support. Historical adapter/probe fields remain historical; actual full source reader, target exclusion, tokens, throughput, group/heldout coverage and final mixture are separate gates.\n\nDRAMP remains preparation only: writer preparation SHA34d291c16e319d5d94da10d9f12cb781948ff933937eadfb767fbd448c6459e4 and root static review059bd184… are preserved. Its actual110-row candidate component is unlaunched and needs a NEW execution supplement/review. Expanded ADMET/ProCyon/X-Pert/retrosynthesis construction remains pending.\n'''
